Subject: [PATCH 08003/11362] [outer-loop] migrate the ARC inducer Qwen3.6-27B
 -> gemma-4-31B-it: 11-0-2 head-to-head, MTP is real, and the
 object-perception metric turns out to be at an instrument floor

THE HEAD-TO-HEAD. gemma-4-31B-it beats Qwen3.6-27B-base at held-out world-model
induction on the 13 games where both arms ran (exp6021). The artifact reports THREE
pairings deliberately, and all three point the same way:

  B  fail-as-zero (a cell that produced no usable engine scores 0.0)
       11-0-2, sign test p=0.000977. Mean held-out 0.384 vs 0.063.
       The OPERATIONAL question: hand the inducer an unseen game, what do you get?
  A  scorable-only (average only over cells that produced an engine at all)
       8-1-1, p=0.039062. Mean 0.388 vs 0.156.
       Controls for the budget confound -- every one of Qwen's 18 non-scorable
       cells overran the identical 16384-token budget -- but averages over UNEQUAL
       trial counts, so it is noisier on Qwen's side than a per-game mean implies.
  C  strict, both arms scored ALL trials
       3-0-1, p=0.25, NOT significant at 0.05. Same direction as A and B.
       Quoting only A and B would be selective, so C is stated here too. Note its
       own min_reachable_p_at_this_d is also 0.25: at 3 discordant games
       significance was UNREACHABLE by construction, so "not significant" here is a
       statement about the sample size, not evidence against the effect. C is a
       robustness check, never the headline -- it discards exactly the games one arm
       failed on, which are the most informative ones.

PLACEMENT. gemma-4-31B-it Q4_K_M fits on ONE RTX 3090 at the shipped n_ctx 81920
only with q8_0 KV. Measured, not assumed: at f16 KV it does not fit, and the two
escape hatches were both measured and REJECTED --

  - FFN offload to host: works, but pushes ~14 blocks off-GPU at 81920 and the
    decode cost is not worth it (results/arc_gemma31b_migration_evidence_20260728/
    ffn_offload_results.json).
  - the AMD iGPU: measured at 1.92 tok/s decode via the HIP llama-server build
    (igpu_throughput.json). ~26x slower than the 3090 path. Not viable for the
    scored envelope.

MTP IS REAL, AND IT IS A SEPARATE FILE. The prior note in this repo assumed
gemma-4-31B-it could self-draft. It cannot: the main GGUF declares no
nextn_predict_layers. The MTP head ships as a distinct 491 MiB
mtp-gemma-4-31B-it-Q8_0.gguf under MTP/ in the same repo. The old warning about
`--model-draft <the main weights>` was therefore exactly right and is preserved --
pointing --model-draft at the main GGUF loads the 18.3 GB weights TWICE. Verified on
the SHIPPED Kaggle binary, not just locally: draft_n_accepted 319 of 576 drafted
tokens, 50.6 tok/s with MTP on vs 35.9 off, a 1.4x decode floor
(mtp_shipped_binary_t1/shipped_mtp_{on,off}.json).

FIVE FIXES THE MIGRATION FORCED.
  1. The VRAM guard had no MTP term at all. Fitted from two measured points
     (862 MiB at n_ctx 32768, 1290 at 81920) to
     head_mib = 576.6 + 0.008708 * n_ctx.
  2. kv_quant was not being carried through as q8_0 -- the one setting the 81920
     placement depends on.
  3. repo_substr was matching the wrong snapshot directory.
  4. --model-draft now resolves to the MTP HEAD, never to the main weights file.
     _resolve_gguf must never let a caller fall back to the main GGUF.
  5. ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_MTP_SCORED_DEFAULT had ZERO runtime effect in the Kaggle
     kernel -- it was read but never reached the launch path. Head presence was
     doing all the work. Now it actually gates speculative decoding, and the
     kernel says so out loud when it is off.

HUD-MASK SWALLOW GUARD. A mask that deletes the whole game makes the IDENTITY
engine optimal, so the mask now refuses when the swallow check cannot be evaluated,
under the distinct status refused_swallow_check_unmeasurable rather than silently
counting as `applied`. DEFAULT-OFF, as every flag in this lane remains.

THE OBJECT-PERCEPTION NULL, AND WHY IT IS NOT A CAPABILITY CLAIM. exp6018's
held-out A/B is null -- primary metric zero in BOTH arms, zero discordant pairs, so
no test was possible; acceptance_gate_passed is false and the artifact says
"unmeasurable_instrument_floor" in its own verdict. The POSITIVE CONTROL is what
makes that readable: showing the model every transition INCLUDING the ones the
production prompt withholds, then grading on those same withheld indices, still
yields max_accuracy 0.0 across 28 cells (metric_demonstrably_moves: false), while
cell_recall does move (max 0.443). So the metric cannot register a win even when the
answer is in the prompt. This is an instrument at its floor, not evidence that
object perception does not help. Do not cite it as the latter.

---- ANALYSER REBUILDS: 14 artifacts, and ONE published figure DID move ----

Editing arc_executable_world_model.py / arc_competition_agent.py /
submission_kernel/main.py drifted the analyser-produced artifacts, so 14 were
rebuilt in dependency order. A rebuild re-runs the ANALYSIS over the SAME frozen
rows; it does not re-run any experiment.

A CORRECTION IS OWED on exp6011, and it is stated here rather than left for a
reader to find. The swallow guard moves ft09's three seed rows from `applied` to
`refused_swallow_check_unmeasurable`, which SHRINKS the mask-applied population that
three published summary figures are computed over:

    n_mask_applied                           45  ->  42
    ondisk_delta_mask_resolved_only.mean      0.16037  ->  0.171825
    identity_delta_mask_resolved_only.mean    0.323148 ->  0.34623

Both means RISE, and the direction is expected rather than surprising: ft09's corpus
is all no-ops, so the identity engine scores 1.0 masked or unmasked and its delta is
0 by construction. Dropping three zero-delta rows from the denominator raises the
mean. The pooled-over-75 figure (0.096222) is UNCHANGED -- it never conditioned on
the mask applying. Zero `passed` values moved, so "0 admissions flipped" still holds.
hud_mask_status_counts now resolves four distinct statuses (applied 42, unresolved
24, refused_swallows_dynamics 6, refused_swallow_check_unmeasurable 3) where it
previously collapsed the last two. Full before/after table and rationale are in
ops/verifier_gaps.md corrigendum item 5.

Everything else that moved, stated separately from clock churn:
  - exp6011: 7537 ADDED leaves (the new hud_mask_swallow diagnostic block), 42
    substantive row-level moves (ft09 rows 15-17), plus the aggregate above.
  - exp6013: 30 substantive row-level moves (ft09 rows 33-35), 0 added. It has NO
    summary block, so it correctly shows no aggregate move -- consistent, not a
    missed recomputation.
  - exp6012: 2640 added leaves, 0 substantive moves.
  - The other 11: clocks, hashes and dates only. Two carry a downstream hash
    citation that moved BECAUSE its upstream was correctly rebuilt first
    (llm_on_wallclock_envelope cites lever_ab's sha256; generator_concurrency_fix
    quotes the reset-attribution recapture wall time in prose).
  - A 12th artifact, outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore_20260726, was fresh at
    the start and became stale BECAUSE the first rebuilds changed artifacts it
    fingerprints as row sources. Rebuilt last. Two more,
    outer_loop_arc_max_actions_answer and outer_loop_arc_reset_charge_attribution,
    were also rebuilt; both diff to zero substantive moves. 14 touched in total.

NO headline moved: the card-ground-truth result (real median optimism 0.018097 vs
modelled 0.036903, model wrong on 17/44 cells, 6 sign-flipped) and the gateway
rescore (median 0.046236, max 0.168048, 42/44 non-zero) are bit-identical. Two of
the rebuilds are LIVE re-captures rather than re-analyses -- reset-attribution re-ran
18 cells and card-ground-truth re-ran 48 -- and both reproduce their prior numbers
exactly, which is the strongest evidence here that the 31B migration did not change
agent behaviour on those paths.

---- SEVEN HISTORICAL ARTIFACTS WERE BEING REWRITTEN BY `pytest` ITSELF ----

Found while preparing this commit, and it is the reason the rebuild accounting above
can be trusted. Seven committed artifacts had drifted with nothing to do with the
migration -- experiment_1869_hiled (efficiency_gains_ms 4.2827 -> 2.1133, HALVED),
experiment_625/638/645_tier1_fr11_relay (run_date/started_at/finished_at restamped
2026-07-27 -> 2026-07-28, FALSIFYING a historical run date), and
experiment_2736/3583/3611 (duration_s + reproducibility_checksum). All seven have
been reverted to HEAD; none is freshness-registered, so reverting re-stales nothing.

The cause is structural and would have recurred on every future test run:
  - test_hiled_simulator_1869.py wrote a LIVE latency measurement straight to a
    hardcoded absolute path under results/.
  - test_experiment_2736/3583/3611 call the experiment's main()/run(), which resolve
    both inputs and output relative to the CWD -- so running the suite from the repo
    root overwrote the artifact. 3611 additionally did os.remove() on it FIRST, so a
    mid-run failure would have deleted part of the research record outright.
  - scripts/experiment_625/638/645_tier1_fr11_relay.py have NO
    `if __name__ == "__main__"` guard: the entire experiment runs at MODULE IMPORT,
    so merely importing them to test their helpers re-ran the experiment and wrote
    the artifact.
All are now sandboxed (tmp_path + monkeypatch.chdir, or a scoped no-op of
AtomicResultWriter.write across the side-effecting import). Every assertion is
preserved; only the write LOCATION moved. Verified: the full staged test set now
leaves results/ untouched.

test_experiment_3583_archive additionally had a STANDING failure that this exposed --
it asserts n_tasks_archived > 0, but research-complete.yaml has been rotated and no
longer contains milestone 2026.05.329 at all, so the count is 0 and the committed
artifact itself records 0. It now seeds a deterministic fixture and asserts the exact
count, testing the script's counting logic instead of the mutable contents of a
rotating ops file.

---- RUFF EXCLUSION: KEY ON THE FILE NAME, NOT THE DIRECTORY ----

[tool.ruff] extend-exclude grows to cover results/**/world_model.py. Keying on the
DIRECTORY had now failed four times running (arc_e3 -> arc_e3_origin_fixtures ->
.../e3 -> e3_store / e3_positive_control): the directory is named by whichever
experiment wrote it and there is no convention to rely on. The FILE name is the real
invariant -- all 437 tracked results/**/world_model.py are LLM-authored engine
stores, verified across every such directory, with no hand-written counterexample.
It is also NARROWER than a directory glob: real analyser code under results/ (e.g.
results/first_win_llm_on_20260727/build_artifact.py, itself a freshness dependency)
stays linted. Without this, ruff would have reformatted 136 generated engines in this
commit alone, and reformatting frozen evidence destroys the property that makes it
evidence.

results/arc_gemma31b_migration_evidence_20260728 is also excluded, as a preserved
measurement harness that must stay byte-identical to what executed. The pyproject
comment now discloses ALL 149 findings that hides, not just the two that blocked the
commit -- including 16 F821 undefined-name, which is a CORRECTNESS class and so was
inspected rather than waved through. All 16 are false positives of an exec()-based
globals injection (phase1b.py:31 and phase1c_mtp.py:16 exec fitgrid.py's source into
module globals; Sampler, http and wait_for_card are all defined there). Ruff cannot
see through exec(). The harnesses do run, and did.

