---- TWO TEST FIXTURES DELIBERATELY NOT MIGRATED ----

The Qwen3.5-9B-MTP -> gemma-4-31B-it rename sweep was over-broad. It rewrote the
fixtures in test_experiment_4994_ and test_experiment_4939_heldout_first_win_readiness,
which stand in for the FROZEN historical artifacts exp4983/4972/4928 -- all three
still carry model_specs.name == "Qwen3.5-9B-MTP" on disk. Re-pinning the live stack
does not retroactively change what a past experiment ran on. Both fixtures are
reverted and commented; the module gates were left INTACT rather than relaxed (4994's
_source_blocker() asserts on that exact value; 4939's module calls it "the methodology
stamp whose absence caused the historical flag" but has no equality assert, so its
identical corruption was passing silently).

---- ONE QA-LAYER FIX ----

adversarial_verify's TAUTOLOGY check fired CRITICAL on duration_s vs
measurement_wall_s. Those are NESTED spans -- process wall time physically contains
the summed per-row measurement spans -- so they agree to 5+ significant figures by
construction, differing only by sub-millisecond bookkeeping overhead. A CRITICAL there
would have stamped flagged_adversarial on three honest artifacts and excluded them
from capstone aggregation. Raising the emitted precision 3dp -> 6dp did NOT fix it and
could not; re-running until the timings differed would be dodging the detector rather
than satisfying it. So the fix is a carve-out in _legitimate_pair, anchored to that
exact named pair -- NOT a blanket exemption for duration fields, since two unrelated
durations coinciding is still real copy-paste evidence. Corpus-wide check: of 15282
artifacts, 13 carry both fields and exactly ONE changes verdict -- the one that was
falsely flagged. Six regression tests pin it, three of them guarding that unrelated
duration pairs and distinct outcome metrics stay CRITICAL.

Also fixed: _rel_or_abs in the three exp601x scripts now resolve()s before
relative_to. This environment exposes the repo under two names, and invoking a rebuild
from the .../Carnot-EBM/carnot-ebm symlink alias silently rewrote
provenance.engine_store to an absolute machine-specific path on what should have been
a no-op rebuild. Verified end-to-end: the same $PWD invocation from the alias now
keeps engine_store repo-relative and engine_store_is_frozen_fixtures true. The three
rebuild_command strings no longer say $PWD.

Nothing submitted, nothing pushed, no Kaggle interaction. All 89 SUBMITTED_* /
MAX_ACTIONS declarations are byte-identical to HEAD, including the submitted
per-game loop guard MAX_ACTIONS = 400 (arc_competition_agent.py:6670; the
module-level MAX_ACTIONS = 200 at :117 is a different, also-unchanged constant) and
SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE = None. artifact-freshness-lint OK (16/16), determination-preservation
OK, adversarial_verify clean over all 14 rebuilds (the single WARN on
first_win_llm_on_eval_concurrency is pre-existing and byte-identical at HEAD).

